# Convert decompilable LMLM mods into open SHAR mod packages

Keep the compatibility tool in the Rust-only `tools/lmlm/` boundary.
It requires Rust 1.97.1 and does not install or bootstrap a toolchain. It
extracts an eligible legacy LMLM package, reconstructs an inspectable open
conversion workspace, and reports what still needs adaptation
to the final SHAR mod-package schema.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Keep conversion completely outside the faithful base pipeline.
- [x] Default converter policy to `decompilable-mods-only=true`; treat that one
  local policy as authoritative. Any user change is an explicit local decision,
  and the user assumes responsibility for the content they inspect, convert,
  modify, or redistribute.
- [x] Test first with the local Jebano and Muckluck packages as fixtures, without
  auto-installing or auto-injecting either mod into the game.
- [x] Never promise arbitrary LMLM compatibility; unsupported legacy behavior
  must be reported so authors can adapt the resulting open package.
- [ ] Produce inspectable SHAR packages whose assets and source are not intentionally
  locked or obfuscated; packaging format follows the final shared mod contract.
- [x] Preserve provenance and require users/distributors to have rights to the
  content they convert or redistribute.
- [x] Update README conversion instructions and known limitations whenever the
  converter contract changes.

## Dependencies

Depends on the new SHAR mod-package schema and removal of LMLM from base input.

## Evidence

`tools/lmlm/` is now a Rust 1.97.1 boundary with strict LSPA v5 parsing,
read-only inspection, atomic open-workspace conversion, and SHA-256
source/per-file evidence. Shared P3D, filesystem, CLI, and SHA-256 behavior is
reused from existing repository crates instead of duplicated. It has no dependency on the
base extraction/build pipeline or the original game installation.

Synthetic Rust tests cover path safety, portable collisions, payload overlap,
zero-padding, atomic publication, overwrite refusal, folder-driven WIP/export
reuse, shared P3D decompilation, and CLI behavior. Read-only `inspect` also
validated the local Jebano `j.lmlm` (1,540 entries, 7 valid P3D payloads) and
Muckluck `m.lmlm` (32 entries, 29 valid P3D payloads) inputs without installing
either package. An architecture guard rejects any LMLM reference under `src/`. The compatibility
tool remains outside the reconstruction pipeline. Folder-driven conversion uses `tools/lmlm/import/`,
preserves WIP state under `.cache/lmlm/wip/`, and publishes local results under
`tools/lmlm/export/`. Final SHAR package adaptation remains open until the
mod-package schema is authoritative.
